	"notes": "This is Apple's homepage, and it is built the way most marketing sites are: a stack of full-width colour bands, one for the glowing-logo hero, one for the 'College, sorted' promo, each running edge to edge. The surprising thing only shows up in the numbers, not the picture: the content inside those bands stays exactly as wide as the browser all the way up to a 1920px desktop screen, and only on the widest ultrawide monitor tested here does it finally stop growing and lock to about 2560 pixels, with the extra room turning into quiet margin on both sides. The hero band is also unusually tall — about three screens' worth in the code — which is the usual sign that the apple logo and headline animate in as you scroll, rather than sitting still as one picture. On a phone, the whole top menu collapses into a single hamburger icon, and every band still stacks into one plain column.",
